        <div class="column">
          <section id="about">
            <h2>About</h2>
            <p>
              I recently graduated cum laude with distinction from the University of Pennsylvania, where I studied Philosophy, Politics, and Economics and minored in Environmental Studies. My interests include digital journalism, political communication, and the intersection of media, politics, and culture. My honors thesis explored how Democratic Party culture shapes the use of celebrities in political campaigns. I formerly worked as a Social Video intern at Morning Brew, producing news content across platforms, and currently work in congressional communications. Outside of work, I write and perform sketch and stand-up comedy. I was the first female Chair of Mask and Wig in the organization's 138-year history and also performed with Simply Chaos.
            </p>
            <p>
              Looking ahead, I hope to work in the entertainment and political news space, ideally in research, writing, or representation.
            </p>
